{
    "test_name": "MOB.346_Work_Scheduled_View",
    "details": {
        "name": "MOB.346_Work_Scheduled_View",
        "type": "browser",
        "status": "paused",
        "message": "`MOB.346` **The work list's Scheduled view, and the menu item that toggles it** \u2014 both\npreviously untested and unlisted.\n- **Settles which view is the default.** `scheduledView` defaults to `true` and the\n  `Admin` role is `SCHEDULED`, so a fresh Datadog session renders **ScheduledWork** \u2014\n  meaning every other work-list test has been running against it, and `AssignedWork` is\n  the view nothing exercises. Leg 1 proves it rather than assuming it.\n- **Asserts `Today` and `Tomorrow` only.** Those two groups set `hideWhenEmpty: false`,\n  so they render on an EMPTY list \u2014 and the `Admin` crew's list is empty on dev. `Past\n  Due`/`Future` would make this a fixture test.\n- **The negative leg is the proof**: after toggling, those headers must be GONE. Without\n  it a no-op toggle would pass (trap 5).\n- **SELF-RESTORING**, restore leg `alwaysExecute` \u2014 `toggle_mobile_v_work` is\n  sessionStorage and a suite shares one browser session, the same hazard as the two map\n  toggles (MOB.341, MOB.585).\n- Proof is `sessionStorage`, the app's own contract, not the icon (trap 16).",
        "tags": [
            "Mobile",
            "env:dev",
            "Work Orders",
            "Scheduled",
            "read-only"
        ],
        "locations": [
            "gcp:us-west2"
        ],
        "config": {
            "assertions": [],
            "config_variables": [
                {
                    "id": "fe7958bf-435f-4932-af8e-0931caab79e7",
                    "name": "MOBDEV",
                    "type": "global"
                }
            ],
            "request": {
                "headers": {},
                "method": "GET",
                "url": "{{ MOBDEV }}"
            },
            "variables": [
                {
                    "id": "fe7958bf-435f-4932-af8e-0931caab79e7",
                    "name": "MOBDEV",
                    "type": "global"
                }
            ],
            "set_cookie": ""
        },
        "options": {
            "device_ids": [
                "chrome.tablet"
            ],
            "disable_cors": false,
            "disable_csp": false,
            "ignore_server_certificate_error": false,
            "min_failure_duration": 0,
            "min_location_failed": 1,
            "monitor_options": {},
            "no_screenshot": false,
            "retry": {
                "count": 1,
                "interval": 300.0
            },
            "rum_settings": {
                "is_enabled": false
            },
            "tick_every": 86400
        },
        "steps": [
            {
                "allowFailure": false,
                "alwaysExecute": false,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": true,
                "name": "Navigate to /work \u2014 the work order list",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "value": "https://dev.mentorapm.com/apm-mobile/work"
                },
                "type": "goToUrl"
            },
            {
                "allowFailure": false,
                "alwaysExecute": false,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": true,
                "name": "Let the work list begin rendering",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "value": 3
                },
                "type": "wait"
            },
            {
                "allowFailure": false,
                "alwaysExecute": false,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": true,
                "name": "The \"Work Orders\" page mounted",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "check": "contains",
                    "value": "Work Orders",
                    "element": {
                        "url": "https://dev.mentorapm.com/apm-mobile/work",
                        "userLocator": {
                            "failTestOnCannotLocate": true,
                            "values": [
                                {
                                    "type": "xpath",
                                    "value": "//*[@id=\"page-title\"]//h4[contains(normalize-space(.), \"Work Orders\")]"
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    }
                },
                "type": "assertElementContent",
                "timeout": 30
            },
            {
                "allowFailure": true,
                "alwaysExecute": true,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": false,
                "name": "DIAG: open the menu to read the toggle's label",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "element": {
                        "url": "https://dev.mentorapm.com/apm-mobile/work",
                        "userLocator": {
                            "failTestOnCannotLocate": true,
                            "values": [
                                {
                                    "type": "xpath",
                                    "value": "//button[@aria-label=\"Toggle navigation\"]"
                                }
                            ]
                        }
                    }
                },
                "type": "click",
                "timeout": 30
            },
            {
                "allowFailure": false,
                "alwaysExecute": true,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": true,
                "name": "Let the menu open",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "value": 1
                },
                "type": "wait"
            },
            {
                "allowFailure": true,
                "alwaysExecute": true,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": false,
                "name": "DIAG A: the toggle item is ABSENT \u2014 the role is NOT 'SCHEDULED'",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "code": "const t = document.body.innerText || '';\nreturn !/Toggle Work Order (List|Scheduled) View/.test(t);"
                },
                "type": "assertFromJavascript",
                "timeout": 10
            },
            {
                "allowFailure": true,
                "alwaysExecute": true,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": false,
                "name": "DIAG B: label reads 'List' \u2014 scheduledView is TRUE, scheduled view is ACTIVE",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "code": "const t = document.body.innerText || '';\nreturn /Toggle Work Order List View/.test(t);"
                },
                "type": "assertFromJavascript",
                "timeout": 10
            },
            {
                "allowFailure": true,
                "alwaysExecute": true,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": false,
                "name": "DIAG C: label reads 'Scheduled' \u2014 scheduledView is FALSE, plain list is up",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "code": "const t = document.body.innerText || '';\nreturn /Toggle Work Order Scheduled View/.test(t);"
                },
                "type": "assertFromJavascript",
                "timeout": 10
            },
            {
                "allowFailure": false,
                "alwaysExecute": true,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": true,
                "name": "Close the menu again",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "value": "Escape"
                },
                "type": "pressKey"
            },
            {
                "allowFailure": false,
                "alwaysExecute": true,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": true,
                "name": "Let the menu close",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "value": 1
                },
                "type": "wait"
            },
            {
                "allowFailure": true,
                "alwaysExecute": true,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": false,
                "name": "DIAG D: how many scheduled-group headers are on screen (>=1?)",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "code": "const bs = [...document.querySelectorAll('button')].filter(b => /^(Past Due|Today|Tomorrow|Future)/.test((b.textContent||'').trim()));\nreturn bs.length >= 1;"
                },
                "type": "assertFromJavascript",
                "timeout": 10
            },
            {
                "allowFailure": true,
                "alwaysExecute": true,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": false,
                "name": "DIAG E: a group header exists but NOT as a button (locator would be wrong)",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "code": "const t = document.body.innerText || '';\nconst bs = [...document.querySelectorAll('button')].filter(b => /^(Past Due|Today|Tomorrow|Future)/.test((b.textContent||'').trim()));\nreturn /\\bTomorrow\\b/.test(t) && bs.length === 0;"
                },
                "type": "assertFromJavascript",
                "timeout": 10
            },
            {
                "allowFailure": true,
                "alwaysExecute": false,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": true,
                "name": "SCHEDULED VIEW: at least one group header is rendered (readiness gate) \u2014 NON-CRITICAL: if the role is not SCHEDULED this fails alone rather than aborting the suite; read DIAG A to tell the two apart",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "code": "const bs = [...document.querySelectorAll('button')].filter(b => /^(Past Due|Today|Tomorrow|Future)\\b/.test((b.textContent||'').trim()));\nconst n = bs.length;\nconst withCount = bs.filter(b => /\\(\\d+\\)/.test(b.textContent||'')).length;\nreturn n >= 1;"
                },
                "type": "assertFromJavascript",
                "timeout": 120
            },
            {
                "allowFailure": false,
                "alwaysExecute": false,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": true,
                "name": "DEFAULT: sessionStorage has no toggle yet, or holds 'true'",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "code": "const v = sessionStorage.getItem('toggle_mobile_v_work');\nreturn v === null || v === 'true';"
                },
                "type": "assertFromJavascript",
                "timeout": 30
            },
            {
                "allowFailure": false,
                "alwaysExecute": false,
                "exitIfSucceed": false,
                "isCritical": true,
                "name": "SCHEDULED VIEW: every rendered group header carries its (count)",
                "noScreenshot": false,
                "params": {
                    "code": "const bs = [...document.querySelectorAll('button')].filter(b => /^(Past Due|Today|Tomorrow|Future)\\b/.test((b.textContent||'').trim()));\nconst n = bs.length;\nconst withCount = bs.filter(b => /\\(\\d+\\)/.test(b.textContent||'')).length;\nreturn n >= 1 && n === withCount;"
                },
                "type": "assertFromJavascript",
                "timeout": 60
            },
